/-!
# Finite-type relative ampleness and common very ample powers

Source: Stacks Project, Morphisms, Tags 01VU and 01VR, with Definitions 01VH and 01VM
(blueprint: lem-trf-relative-ample-very-ample).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- Over a quasi-compact base, a finite-type morphism has the stated equivalences between
relative ampleness, one positive relatively very ample power, and eventual relative very
ampleness. The final clause applies independently to every quasi-compact g over X.
The evaluation arrow is the counit of the section-normalized tensor adjunction, and
`IsCanonicalMap` identifies the associated morphism by its homogeneous-fraction formula.

Source: Stacks Project, Morphisms, Tags 01VU and 01VR (clause (4)), Definitions 01VH, 01VM
(blueprint: lem-trf-relative-ample-very-ample).

Proof, following the node's eight steps:
1. Local projective-bundle immersion witnesses make g separated: bundle projections
are separated by lem-trf-projective-bundle-quotient-geometry, and immersions are separated
by def-weil-closed-immersion, lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-integral-separated-uc and
lem-weil-pbc-open-immersion-monomorphism. Composition and target locality use
lem-weil-pbc-proper-fp-permanence and lem-weil-pbc-closed-finite-etale-zariski-local.
Then lem-pc-separated-quasi-separated makes g quasi-separated.
2. Invertibility makes N quasi-coherent, and pqf-lem-pushforward-qcoh makes g_*N
quasi-coherent. A local quotient g_j^*E_j to N is the evaluation counit composed with
the pullback of its adjoint, by lem-pc-module-pullback-adjunction. Thus evaluation is
surjective locally, hence globally. The quotient geometry constructs its canonical map.
3. The adjoint E_j to (g_*N)|V_j induces a quotient on an open U_j in P(g_*N)|V_j.
This open is the union of the nonvanishing loci of the images of local sections in the
tautological line (def-weil-pbc-ample-invertible-module). The counit factorization makes
the canonical map land in U_j; the quotient bijection identifies its composite with the
original immersion. Apply lem-zl-immersion-cancellation, composition permanence, and
lem-zl-immersion-near-image-locality. This proves the final assertion without finite type.
4. A finite affine cover of X exists by lem-weil-pbc-qcqs-finite-affine-open-cover.
On each inverse image the ample restriction has one positive very ample power, by
lem-weil-pbc-ample-very-ample-immersion-affine-base. Identify projective spaces and twists
with projective bundles via lem-trf-projective-bundle-quotient-geometry. Empty pieces use
power one and the empty immersion into projective zero-space.
5. By lem-weil-pbc-coherent-twist-global-generation the remaining sufficiently large
powers are generated by finitely many sections. Combine that quotient map with the
one-power immersion and apply the Segre closed immersion (lem-chow-segre, def-chow-segre).
Its coordinates multiply, so lem-weil-pbc-invertible-pullback-tensor identifies the pulled
back twist with the desired power. Immersion cancellation and composition give immersion.
6. Take the maximum of one and the finitely many local bounds. Steps 1--3 globalize the
local very ample witnesses for every power above that bound. Including one handles the
empty cover and empty base.
7. Conversely a very ample power gives a degree-one quotient. Extend by the symmetric
algebra universal property (def-trf-canonical-symmetric-graded-algebra and
lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-symmetric-algebra). Its graded map is generated everywhere
and induces the original immersion by quotient geometry. Apply
lem-trf-graded-immersion-ample-criterion to get ampleness over every affine open.
8. Positive-power reflection follows directly from def-weil-pbc-ample-invertible-module:
a section of (L^n)^k is the same section of L^(n*k), with the same nonvanishing locus,
and n*k is positive. Finally eventual very ampleness supplies a positive example by
choosing an exponent at least both one and the bound. -/
theorem relative_ample_very_ample {Y X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ X)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f] [CompactSpace X]
    (M : Y.Modules) [M.IsInvertible] :
    (((QuasiCompact f ∧ ∀ V : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen V →
        ∃ hM : ((tensorPullback (f ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι).obj M).IsInvertible,
          @IsAmple (f ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme ((tensorPullback (f ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι).obj M) hM) ↔
      ∃ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n ∧ IsRelativelyVeryAmple f (M.tensorPow n)) ∧
    ((QuasiCompact f ∧ ∀ V : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen V →
        ∃ hM : ((tensorPullback (f ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι).obj M).IsInvertible,
          @IsAmple (f ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme ((tensorPullback (f ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι).obj M) hM) ↔
      ∃ n₀ : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, n₀ ≤ n → IsRelativelyVeryAmple f (M.tensorPow n))) ∧
    (∀ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (g : Z ⟶ X) [QuasiCompact g]
      (N : Z.Modules) [N.IsInvertible], IsRelativelyVeryAmple g N →
        QuasiSeparated g ∧ Epi ((tensorPullbackSectionAdjunction g).counit.app N) ∧
        ∃ hF : ((pushforward g).obj N).IsQuasicoherent,
          ∃ r : Z ⟶ (@SymmetricAlgebraSheaf.gradedAlgebraData X
            ((pushforward g).obj N) hF).relProj,
              r ≫ (@SymmetricAlgebraSheaf.gradedAlgebraData X
                ((pushforward g).obj N) hF).relProjHom = g ∧
              @ProjectiveBundleQuotientGeometry.IsCanonicalMap X ((pushforward g).obj N)
                hF Z g N ((tensorPullbackSectionAdjunction g).counit.app N) r ∧
              IsImmersion r) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
